<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr PPI 9.4 pct in June vs 9.7 in May.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr PPI 9.4 pct in June vs 9.7 in May.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish producer prices rose 0.3 percent in June against a 0.4 percent rise in May, taking year-on-year producer price inflation down to 9.4 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>It said PPI rose 4.5 percent in the January-June period, compared with a 5.7 percent rise in the corresponding period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH PRODUCER INFLATION	    JUNE	 MAY     JUNE 96</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)		0.3	 0.4	  0.8</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)			9.4	 9.7(9.6)  13.4</p>
<p>  manufacturing m/m change	     0.3	 0.5(0.4)   0.7</p>
<p>  manufacturing yr/yr change	   8.0	 8.2	 10.8</p>
<p>  mining m/m change			0.5	 0.6(0.4)   2.1</p>
<p>  mining yr/yr change		   17.2	18.3(18.0) 12.0</p>
<p>  utilities m/m change		   0.1	 0.2(0.1)   0.2</p>
<p>  utilities yr/yr change		11.1	11.1(9.3)  18.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in brackets were revised.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
